Goal:
To obtain the password by setting up a listener on port with the current level's password and then
using the setuid file given to us and specifying the port to retrive the password.

Connect:
ssh user@host port

Approach:
. The first step was to know if there was any port that existed that was listening for connection 
  from the setuid file.
. Unfortunately there wasn't any so i had set one up mannually which was to echo the current level 
  password into a netcat listener at a specified port.
.  Then use the setuid file with the port that we just specified and obtain the password.

Command:
echo 'password' | nc -lp 4444 &
./setuid-file 4444

Breakdown:
. The first command is used to setup a listener on the port 4444 with the current level's password.
. The next command is used to check the password on that port if they match we get the password for
  the next level.

Results:
As the password matched we got the password for the next level.

Key-takeaway:
Learnt how to setup a netcat listener on a certain port and background it and then access it to
get the password for the next level.
